1
00:00:00,577 --> 00:00:04,264
hx-boost will take over all anchor elements

2
00:00:04,264 --> 00:00:06,846
that are nested inside of this body element,

3
00:00:07,647 --> 00:00:09,475
but it will actually do more than that.

4
00:00:10,052 --> 00:00:12,858
And for that, I'll copy it and also bring it

5
00:00:12,858 --> 00:00:15,631
to my second page and then there to the body

6
00:00:16,642 --> 00:00:19,175
so that it for one will also control this

7
00:00:19,255 --> 00:00:22,013
anchor element, but so that it will also

8
00:00:22,061 --> 00:00:23,776
control this form

9
00:00:24,802 --> 00:00:27,640
because hx-boost will not just change the

10
00:00:27,688 --> 00:00:29,163
behavior of anchor

11
00:00:29,773 --> 00:00:31,345
but also of forms.

12
00:00:32,163 --> 00:00:34,425
And it will change it such that it takes a

13
00:00:34,425 --> 00:00:36,575
look at the method of a form, which you

14
00:00:36,671 --> 00:00:38,436
therefore need to specify,

15
00:00:39,302 --> 00:00:40,329
and the action.

16
00:00:41,404 --> 00:00:43,810
And it will then either send a GET or a POST

17
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:46,826
request depending on the method to that path

18
00:00:46,859 --> 00:00:47,051
here.

19
00:00:47,837 --> 00:00:50,516
So in the end, you can think of it replacing

20
00:00:50,693 --> 00:00:52,907
this method-action combination we have here

21
00:00:53,356 --> 00:00:56,429
with hx-post send to

22
00:00:57,610 --> 00:00:57,917
/cart.

23
00:00:59,649 --> 00:01:02,367
We don't have to add that manually because

24
00:01:02,545 --> 00:01:05,505
hx-boost will essentially replace this

25
00:01:05,779 --> 00:01:08,074
method-action combination with that

26
00:01:08,204 --> 00:01:09,206
attribute, you could say.

27
00:01:10,050 --> 00:01:12,089
And therefore, of course, the respective

28
00:01:12,332 --> 00:01:15,311
route on the backend will be triggered and

29
00:01:15,505 --> 00:01:18,484
HTMX will then take the response from that

30
00:01:18,484 --> 00:01:21,216
route and again update the entire page. So

31
00:01:21,216 --> 00:01:23,077
it will still give you that single page

32
00:01:23,077 --> 00:01:24,087
application feeling.

33
00:01:24,761 --> 00:01:27,713
For form submissions, it just won't update

34
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:28,322
the URL.

35
00:01:28,932 --> 00:01:30,873
But we can see it in action here by adding a

36
00:01:30,873 --> 00:01:33,311
new route to this demo application here,

37
00:01:34,531 --> 00:01:37,755
a POST route for /cart since that is what I

38
00:01:37,755 --> 00:01:39,086
specified in that form.

39
00:01:40,562 --> 00:01:43,193
And then there we could store some cart data

40
00:01:43,225 --> 00:01:46,033
if this were a real app, but here I'll just

41
00:01:46,273 --> 00:01:47,749
send back a response.

42
00:01:48,507 --> 00:01:50,508
And specifically here, I in the end wanna

43
00:01:50,508 --> 00:01:53,477
redirect to the starting page. So I'll send

44
00:01:53,574 --> 00:01:55,768
back the content of the starting page in the

45
00:01:55,768 --> 00:01:58,877
end since HTMX will follow redirects as you

46
00:01:58,877 --> 00:01:59,259
learned.

47
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:03,382
And therefore with this route added here, if

48
00:02:03,382 --> 00:02:04,463
you save everything,

49
00:02:05,141 --> 00:02:08,223
if you go to such a product detail page and

50
00:02:08,223 --> 00:02:09,772
you click on Add to Cart,

51
00:02:10,305 --> 00:02:12,331
you see we're back on the starting page.

52
00:02:13,777 --> 00:02:17,006
Now, as you see, the URL did now change

53
00:02:17,086 --> 00:02:19,946
because HTMX detected that we redirected.

54
00:02:20,524 --> 00:02:23,335
And in that case, a new GET request was sent

55
00:02:23,496 --> 00:02:25,681
after the POST request. And for GET

56
00:02:25,681 --> 00:02:27,930
requests, like the ones triggered by

57
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:30,050
clicking anchor elements, but also GET

58
00:02:30,163 --> 00:02:32,444
requests triggered due to a redirection,

59
00:02:33,135 --> 00:02:35,287
HTMX will update the URL.

60
00:02:36,428 --> 00:02:38,693
But as you can see here, and as you can also

61
00:02:38,757 --> 00:02:41,086
confirm if you click this button again, the

62
00:02:41,102 --> 00:02:43,426
URL never changes to

63
00:02:43,971 --> 00:02:46,086
/cart and that would be the path of this

64
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:48,682
form. So that is what I meant when I said

65
00:02:48,795 --> 00:02:51,936
that it will not update the URL when a form

66
00:02:51,936 --> 00:02:52,529
is submitted.

67
00:02:53,138 --> 00:02:54,757
It will actually update it if you then

68
00:02:54,805 --> 00:02:56,760
navigate to a different page, but it will

69
00:02:56,872 --> 00:02:59,645
not update it with the path defined on the

70
00:02:59,693 --> 00:03:02,241
form. Nonetheless, it will send that

71
00:03:02,241 --> 00:03:05,030
request, follow that redirect here, and

72
00:03:05,062 --> 00:03:07,450
therefore do everything you want it to do

73
00:03:07,706 --> 00:03:09,597
and still give you that single page

74
00:03:09,773 --> 00:03:10,831
application feeling.
